-- חוזר לבעלויות תשע"ג/2: עדכונים לגבי הסכם עוז לתמורה ביישום חלקי בשנה"ל תשע"ג (15.10.2012)
-- What changes for partial implementation of Oz LaTmura in the upper
-- division in school year 2012/13, against the 2011/12 rules of circular
-- תשע"ב/7: the teacher's week, the mother's position, matriculation and
-- homeroom hours in school, the position ceilings, the Oz LaTmura addition,
-- the principal's week and addition, the job bases for the hourly value, the
-- '94 and '87 shekel additions from 27.8.2012, new teachers in upper
-- divisions that have not joined, and new principals and deputies.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `תשע"ג/2 עדכונים לגבי הסכם עוז לתמורה ביישום חלקי בשנה"ל תשע"ג`

-- akn:preamble The letterhead, title (printed run together with the addressee and subject line), date (15.10.2012), and the lead-in: circular תשע"ב/7 published the 2011/12 rules for partial and full implementation, the agreement sets other terms for 2012/13, and the updated terms follow; no rule of its own.

@desc How the Oz LaTmura reform applies to an employee's upper division in 2012/13.
DECLARE `Oz implementation` IS ONE OF
    `not under the reform`
    `partial implementation`
    `full implementation`

@desc The roles the circular distinguishes.
DECLARE `upper-division role` IS ONE OF
    `a teacher`
    `a principal`
    `a deputy principal`

@desc A teaching employee of an owner's upper division in school year 2012/13, as far as this circular asks about it.
DECLARE `upper-division employee` HAS
    `in the upper-division teaching-staff grade` IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed by an owner supervised by the Ministry` IS A BOOLEAN
    `implementation`                     IS AN `Oz implementation` @desc the terms the employee is employed on in 2012/13
    `role`                               IS AN `upper-division role`
    `appointed in 2012/13`               IS A BOOLEAN @desc a principal or deputy newly appointed to the post in 2012/13
    `age`                                IS A NUMBER
    `a mother`                           IS A BOOLEAN @desc a teaching employee who is a mother (section 2(ד))
    `a mother keeping the regular week`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc a mother who goes on working the week she would work were she not a mother (the same number of hours of each kind)
    `actual position`                    IS A NUMBER @desc the share of a full position actually held (1 = 100%)
    `position at all employers`          IS A NUMBER
    `matriculation preparation hours allotted` IS A NUMBER @desc the weekly matriculation-preparation hours allotted to the teacher that year

DECLARE `partial-Oz action` IS ONE OF
    `do matriculation and homeroom hours in school` HAS `hours in school` IS A NUMBER
    `employ on full-implementation terms`
    `pay the management allowance by the pre-reform rules`

§§ `1 תחולה`

@ref akn:art_1/p1
GIVEN e IS AN `upper-division employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `within the scope of section 1` e IF
        e's `in the upper-division teaching-staff grade`
    AND e's `employed by an owner supervised by the Ministry`
    AND e's `implementation` EQUALS `partial implementation`

-- akn:art_1/p2 The heading of the page's section 2 ("עוז לתמורה" in the upper division in partial implementation in 2012/13), which the corpus publishes as a paragraph of section 1; its rules are (א)-(י).

§§ `2 עוז לתמורה בחטיבה העליונה ביישום חלקי בשנה"ל תשע"ג`

-- (א), by section 27(א) of circular תשע"ב/7: a teacher in partial
-- implementation at 100% works in 2012/13 24 frontal hours, 3 individual
-- hours and 5 teaching-support hours (2 for preparing material and grading,
-- 2 for meetings, 1 for receiving parents).
DECLARE `partial-Oz week` HAS
    `frontal teaching hours`    IS A NUMBER
    `individual teaching hours` IS A NUMBER
    `preparation and grading hours` IS A NUMBER
    `meeting hours`             IS A NUMBER
    `parents' hours`            IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:art_1__para_a akn:art_1__para_a/p2
`the full-position week in 2012/13` MEANS
    `partial-Oz week` WITH
        `frontal teaching hours`        IS 24
        `individual teaching hours`     IS 3
        `preparation and grading hours` IS 2
        `meeting hours`                 IS 2
        `parents' hours`                IS 1

GIVEN w IS A `partial-Oz week`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `support hours of` w IS
    w's `preparation and grading hours`
    PLUS w's `meeting hours`
    PLUS w's `parents' hours`

GIVEN w IS A `partial-Oz week`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `weekly hours of` w IS
    w's `frontal teaching hours`
    PLUS w's `individual teaching hours`
    PLUS `support hours of` w

-- The support hours the clause lists add up to the five it states.
#ASSERT `support hours of` `the full-position week in 2012/13` EQUALS 5

-- (ב), by section 27(ה) of circular תשע"ב/7: a mother in partial
-- implementation in 2012/13 who keeps the week she would work were she not a
-- mother is paid by a position 8.3% larger than her actual one.
@ref akn:art_1__para_b
`the mother's addition in 2012/13` MEANS 8.3%

-- F-2012-13_tashag_02-d: "larger by 8.3% than its actual rate" reads as
-- 8.3 points added or as 8.3% of the position added. The reading adopted:
-- points, the reading under which (ד)'s mother's ceiling (139.3%) is the
-- teacher's (131%) plus the addition.
GIVEN e IS AN `upper-division employee`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the position the salary is computed on` e IS
    IF `within the scope of section 1` e AND e's `a mother keeping the regular week`
    THEN e's `actual position` PLUS `the mother's addition in 2012/13`
    ELSE e's `actual position`

`the two readings of the mother's addition differ at 80%` MEANS
    NOT (0.8 PLUS `the mother's addition in 2012/13` EQUALS 0.8 TIMES (1 PLUS `the mother's addition in 2012/13`))
#ASSERT `the two readings of the mother's addition differ at 80%`

-- Only the points reading carries the teacher's ceiling to the mother's.
#ASSERT NOT (131% TIMES (1 PLUS `the mother's addition in 2012/13`) EQUALS 139.3%)

-- (ג), by section 27(ח) of circular תשע"ב/7: in 2012/13 a teacher in
-- partial implementation does in school 2 matriculation-preparation hours
-- out of all those the teacher has, and no more than those allotted that
-- year, and 2 homeroom hours. Time in school weeks.
@ref akn:art_1__para_c akn:art_1__para_c/p2 akn:art_1__para_c/p3 akn:art_1__para_c/p4
`matriculation hours in school in 2012/13` MEANS 2
`homeroom hours in school in 2012/13` MEANS 2

GIVEN e IS AN `upper-division employee`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `matriculation hours done in school` e IS
    min `matriculation hours in school in 2012/13` (e's `matriculation preparation hours allotted`)

GIVEN e IS AN `upper-division employee`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `partial-Oz action`
DECIDE `doing the hours in school` e IS
    IF `within the scope of section 1` e
    THEN PARTY `the teaching employee`
         MUST  `do matriculation and homeroom hours in school` `hours`
               PROVIDED `hours` AT LEAST `matriculation hours done in school` e PLUS `homeroom hours in school in 2012/13`
         LEST BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "section 2(ג): in partial implementation the matriculation and homeroom hours are done in school, in part"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (ד), amending section 28 of circular תשע"ב/7: in 2012/13 the most a
-- teacher in partial implementation may be employed, at all employers
-- together, is 131%, and for a teaching employee who is a mother 139.3%.
@ref akn:art_1__para_d
GIVEN e IS AN `upper-division employee`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the position ceiling in 2012/13` e IS
    IF e's `a mother` THEN 139.3% ELSE 131%

GIVEN e IS AN `upper-division employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `within the position ceiling` e IF
    e's `position at all employers` AT MOST `the position ceiling in 2012/13` e

-- The mother's ceiling is the teacher's plus the mother's addition of (ב).
#ASSERT 131% PLUS `the mother's addition in 2012/13` EQUALS 139.3%

-- (ה), by section 29 of circular תשע"ב/7: the Oz LaTmura addition for
-- teachers in partial implementation in 2012/13 is 21%.
-- (ו) ¶2, by section 32 of circular תשע"ב/7: for existing principals of
-- schools in partial implementation it is 15%. A deputy, a teacher holding
-- a post, takes the teachers' rate, as in (ז).
@ref akn:art_1__para_e akn:art_1__para_f/p2
GIVEN e IS AN `upper-division employee`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the Oz LaTmura addition rate` e IS
    IF `within the scope of section 1` e
    THEN CONSIDER e's `role`
         WHEN `a principal` THEN 15%
         OTHERWISE 21%
    ELSE 0

-- (ו), by section 31 of circular תשע"ב/7: the principal's week in partial
-- implementation (100%) in 2012/13 is 38 hours; 37 for a principal "מגיל
-- 50 ועד …", and a week of its own for one "מגיל 55 ומעלה". The corpus
-- prints the sentence with its figures reordered — "מגיל 50 ועד 36, 55
-- שעות שבועיות" (MMS-426) — so the age at which the band from 50 ends and
-- the hours from 55 are not something its text says: both are named inputs
-- until the corpus is fixed and re-synced. The bands as printed, each with
-- the hours it gives.
@ref akn:art_1__para_f
DECLARE `age band` HAS
    `band role`     IS AN `upper-division role`
    `band from age` IS A NUMBER
    `band to age`   IS A NUMBER @desc 999 stands for "ומעלה"
    `band hours`    IS A NUMBER

@desc Circular 2012-13/2, paragraph 2(ו): the age at which the principal's 37-hour band "from 50" ends. The corpus prints this sentence scrambled (MMS-426), so the value is supplied from outside until the corpus is fixed and re-synced.
ASSUME `the upper age of the principal's band from 50` IS A NUMBER

@desc Circular 2012-13/2, paragraph 2(ו): the weekly hours of a principal "from 55 and above". The corpus prints this sentence scrambled (MMS-426), so the value is supplied from outside until the corpus is fixed and re-synced.
ASSUME `the principal's week from 55` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `upper age of the band from 50` IS A NUMBER
      `hours from 55`                 IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `age band`
DECIDE `the principal's week bands` `upper age of the band from 50` `hours from 55` IS
    LIST `age band` `a principal` 0  49.99 38,
         `age band` `a principal` 50 `upper age of the band from 50` 37,
         `age band` `a principal` 55 999 `hours from 55`

GIVEN bands IS A LIST OF `age band`
      r IS AN `upper-division role`
      a IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `the hours the bands give` bands r a IS
    map (GIVEN b YIELD b's `band hours`)
        (filter (GIVEN b YIELD     b's `band role` EQUALS r
                               AND a AT LEAST b's `band from age`
                               AND a AT MOST b's `band to age`)
                bands)

-- F-2012-13_tashag_02-a, over the inputs: a principal of 55 is in the band
-- from 50 and in the band "from 55 and above", and the two give different
-- weeks. It is asserted on the figures the page prints ("מגיל 50 ועד 55,
-- 36 שעות"), which confirm the finding; no rule uses them.
GIVEN `upper age of the band from 50` IS A NUMBER
      `hours from 55`                 IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a principal of 55 has two weeks` `upper age of the band from 50` `hours from 55` IF
        `the hours the bands give` (`the principal's week bands` `upper age of the band from 50` `hours from 55`) `a principal` 55
            EQUALS LIST 37, `hours from 55`
    AND (NOT (`hours from 55` EQUALS 37))
#ASSERT `a principal of 55 has two weeks` 55 36

-- The reading adopted (F-2012-13_tashag_02-a): the band that opens at 55
-- governs age 55, the band from 50 being read as 50 up to 55.
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the principal's week in 2012/13` a IS
    BRANCH IF a AT LEAST 55 THEN `the principal's week from 55`
           IF a AT LEAST 50 THEN 37
           OTHERWISE 38

-- (ז), by section 33 of circular תשע"ב/7: the job base by which the hourly
-- value is computed in 2012/13 is 32 hours for a teacher and 28 "בגיל 55
-- ומעלה"; for a principal (for an hour of absence) 38, and 36 "בגיל 55
-- ומעלה". Between them each list has a middle band whose ages and hours the
-- corpus prints reordered — "למורה בגיל 30: 50-55ש"ש", "למנהל בגיל 37:
-- 50-55 שעות" (MMS-426) — so which figures are the band's ages and which
-- its hours is not something the text says: the two middle bands are named
-- inputs until the corpus is fixed and re-synced. The base below the middle
-- band applies to those younger than its first age.
`the teacher's job base` MEANS 32
`the principal's job base` MEANS 38

@desc Circular 2012-13/2, paragraph 2(ז): the teacher's middle job-base band — the ages it covers and its weekly hours. The corpus prints this sentence scrambled (MMS-426), so the band is supplied from outside until the corpus is fixed and re-synced.
ASSUME `the teacher's middle job-base band` IS AN `age band`

@desc Circular 2012-13/2, paragraph 2(ז) second paragraph: the principal's middle job-base band — the ages it covers and its weekly hours. The corpus prints this sentence scrambled (MMS-426), so the band is supplied from outside until the corpus is fixed and re-synced.
ASSUME `the principal's middle job-base band` IS AN `age band`

@ref akn:art_1__para_g akn:art_1__para_g/p2
GIVEN `teacher's middle band`   IS AN `age band`
      `principal's middle band` IS AN `age band`
GIVETH A LIST OF `age band`
DECIDE `the job-base bands` `teacher's middle band` `principal's middle band` IS
    LIST `age band` `a teacher`   0  (`teacher's middle band`'s `band from age` MINUS 0.01) `the teacher's job base`,
         `teacher's middle band`,
         `age band` `a teacher`   55 999 28,
         `age band` `a principal` 0  (`principal's middle band`'s `band from age` MINUS 0.01) `the principal's job base`,
         `principal's middle band`,
         `age band` `a principal` 55 999 36

-- F-2012-13_tashag_02-b, over the inputs: at 55 each list puts the
-- employee in its middle band and in the band "from 55 and above", and the
-- two give different bases. It is asserted on the middle bands the page
-- prints ("בגיל 50-55: 30 ש"ש", "בגיל 50-55: 37 שעות"), which confirm the
-- finding; no rule uses them.
GIVEN `teacher's middle band`   IS AN `age band`
      `principal's middle band` IS AN `age band`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the job bases give age 55 two answers` `teacher's middle band` `principal's middle band` IF
        `the hours the bands give` (`the job-base bands` `teacher's middle band` `principal's middle band`) `a teacher` 55
            EQUALS LIST (`teacher's middle band`'s `band hours`), 28
    AND `the hours the bands give` (`the job-base bands` `teacher's middle band` `principal's middle band`) `a principal` 55
            EQUALS LIST (`principal's middle band`'s `band hours`), 36
    AND (NOT (`teacher's middle band`'s `band hours` EQUALS 28))
    AND (NOT (`principal's middle band`'s `band hours` EQUALS 36))

`the teacher's middle band as the page prints it` MEANS `age band` `a teacher` 50 55 30
`the principal's middle band as the page prints it` MEANS `age band` `a principal` 50 55 37
#ASSERT `the job bases give age 55 two answers` `the teacher's middle band as the page prints it` `the principal's middle band as the page prints it`

-- On the page's figures every other whole age from 30 to 70 has one band:
-- 55 is the only overlap.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN a YIELD     count (`the hours the bands give` (`the job-base bands` `the teacher's middle band as the page prints it` `the principal's middle band as the page prints it`) `a teacher` a) EQUALS 1
                           AND count (`the hours the bands give` (`the principal's week bands` 55 36) `a principal` a) EQUALS 1)
            (LIST 30, 40, 49, 50, 51, 52, 53, 54, 56, 60, 65, 70)

-- The reading adopted (F-2012-13_tashag_02-b): the band that opens at 55
-- governs age 55, each middle band being read as running up to 55.
-- (ז) names a teacher's base and a principal's; a deputy, a teacher holding
-- a post, takes the teacher's.
GIVEN `teacher's middle band`   IS AN `age band`
      `principal's middle band` IS AN `age band`
      r IS AN `upper-division role`
      a IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the job base with middle bands` `teacher's middle band` `principal's middle band` r a IS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `a principal` THEN BRANCH IF a AT LEAST 55 THEN 36
                                   IF a AT LEAST `principal's middle band`'s `band from age` THEN `principal's middle band`'s `band hours`
                                   OTHERWISE `the principal's job base`
    OTHERWISE BRANCH IF a AT LEAST 55 THEN 28
                     IF a AT LEAST `teacher's middle band`'s `band from age` THEN `teacher's middle band`'s `band hours`
                     OTHERWISE `the teacher's job base`

@export default The weekly job base by which the hourly value is computed in school year 2012/13 for a teacher or principal in partial implementation of Oz LaTmura in an owner's upper division, under circular תשע"ג/2
GIVEN r IS AN `upper-division role` @desc a teacher or a principal (a deputy is read as a teacher)
      a IS A NUMBER @desc the employee's age in years
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the job base in 2012/13` r a IS
    `the job base with middle bands` `the teacher's middle job-base band` `the principal's middle job-base band` r a

-- The adopted reading agrees with the bands wherever they give one answer
-- (checked on the page's figures), and (א)'s week adds up to the teacher's
-- base.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN a YIELD     `the hours the bands give` (`the job-base bands` `the teacher's middle band as the page prints it` `the principal's middle band as the page prints it`) `a teacher` a
                               EQUALS LIST (`the job base with middle bands` `the teacher's middle band as the page prints it` `the principal's middle band as the page prints it` `a teacher` a))
            (LIST 30, 49, 50, 54, 56, 70)
#ASSERT `weekly hours of` `the full-position week in 2012/13` EQUALS `the teacher's job base`

-- (ח): from 27.8.2012, the '94 teaching-reinforcement and '87 additions.
-- Teachers not on reform terms, and principals on Oz LaTmura terms in full
-- or partial implementation: 153.43 ₪ and 170.62 ₪. Non-principals in
-- partial implementation: 184.42 ₪ and 205.07 ₪. Non-principals in full
-- implementation: unchanged from circular תשע"ב/9 — an input here.
-- F-2012-13_tashag_02-c: the first and third groups are outside section 1's
-- scope.
@ref akn:art_1__para_h akn:art_1__para_h/p2 akn:art_1__para_h/p3 akn:art_1__para_h/p4 akn:art_1__para_h/p5 akn:art_1__para_h/p6 akn:art_1__para_h/p7
DECLARE `shekel additions` HAS
    `the '94 teaching-reinforcement addition` IS A NUMBER
    `the '87 addition`                        IS A NUMBER

ASSUME `the full-implementation amounts of circular תשע"ב/9` IS A `shekel additions`

GIVEN e IS AN `upper-division employee`
GIVETH A `shekel additions`
DECIDE `the shekel additions from 27.8.2012` e IS
    IF e's `implementation` EQUALS `not under the reform` OR e's `role` EQUALS `a principal`
    THEN `shekel additions` 153.43 170.62
    ELSE IF e's `implementation` EQUALS `partial implementation`
         THEN `shekel additions` 184.42 205.07
         ELSE `the full-implementation amounts of circular תשע"ב/9`

-- (ט), a reminder: an upper division that has not joined Oz LaTmura but
-- has new teachers the Ministry found to meet the thresholds employs them on
-- the week and terms of FULL implementation; its tuition budget includes
-- reimbursement by Oz LaTmura's salary costs (by the school's profile) and
-- additional individual and support hours, by those teachers' share of the
-- school's teachers' positions.
@ref akn:art_1__para_i akn:art_1__para_i/p2
GIVEN `the upper division joined` IS A BOOLEAN, `a new teacher meeting the thresholds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `partial-Oz action`
DECIDE `employing a new teacher on full-implementation terms` `the upper division joined` `a new teacher meeting the thresholds` IS
    IF (NOT `the upper division joined`) AND `a new teacher meeting the thresholds`
    THEN PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
         MUST  `employ on full-implementation terms`
         LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "section 2(ט): a new teacher meeting the thresholds is employed on full-implementation terms though the school has not joined"
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref akn:art_1__para_i/p3
GIVEN `the new teachers' positions` IS A NUMBER, `all the school's teachers' positions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the share of the budget on Oz LaTmura terms` `the new teachers' positions` `all the school's teachers' positions` IS
    IF `all the school's teachers' positions` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `the new teachers' positions` DIVIDED BY `all the school's teachers' positions`
    ELSE 0

-- (י): principals and deputies newly appointed in 2012/13 are treated as
-- existing ones: a management allowance by the rules before Oz LaTmura. New
-- principals in full implementation also take the "reform transition
-- addition" of 50% and the "Oz LaTmura addition - principals" of 30%; in
-- partial implementation in 2012/13, 50% and 15%.
@ref akn:art_1__para_j akn:art_1__para_j/p2 akn:art_1__para_j/p3
GIVEN e IS AN `upper-division employee`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `partial-Oz action`
DECIDE `the new appointee's management allowance` e IS
    IF e's `appointed in 2012/13` AND (NOT e's `role` EQUALS `a teacher`)
    THEN PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
         MUST  `pay the management allowance by the pre-reform rules`
         LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "section 2(י): a new principal or deputy is paid the management allowance by the pre-reform rules"
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref akn:art_1__para_j/p4 akn:art_1__para_j/p5
DECLARE `new principal's additions` HAS
    `reform transition addition`     IS A NUMBER
    `Oz LaTmura addition - principals` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN e IS AN `upper-division employee`
GIVETH A `new principal's additions`
DECIDE `the new principal's additions` e IS
    IF e's `appointed in 2012/13` AND e's `role` EQUALS `a principal`
    THEN CONSIDER e's `implementation`
         WHEN `full implementation`    THEN `new principal's additions` (50%) (30%)
         WHEN `partial implementation` THEN `new principal's additions` (50%) (15%)
         OTHERWISE `new principal's additions` 0 0
    ELSE `new principal's additions` 0 0

-- F-2012-13_tashag_02-c: section 1 confines the circular to employees in
-- PARTIAL implementation; (ט) and (י) give rules to new teachers on full-
-- implementation terms and to new principals in full implementation. The
-- reading adopted: each of those clauses governs the case it names.
`a new principal in full implementation` MEANS
    `upper-division employee` WITH
        `in the upper-division teaching-staff grade` IS TRUE
        `employed by an owner supervised by the Ministry` IS TRUE
        `implementation`                     IS `full implementation`
        `role`                               IS `a principal`
        `appointed in 2012/13`               IS TRUE
        `age`                                IS 45
        `a mother`                           IS FALSE
        `a mother keeping the regular week`  IS FALSE
        `actual position`                    IS 1
        `position at all employers`          IS 1
        `matriculation preparation hours allotted` IS 0

`section 2(י) gives additions to an employee outside section 1` MEANS
        (NOT `within the scope of section 1` `a new principal in full implementation`)
    AND (`the new principal's additions` `a new principal in full implementation`)'s `reform transition addition` EQUALS 50%
#ASSERT `section 2(י) gives additions to an employee outside section 1`

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off and signature; no rule.

§§ `Worked examples`

-- A new principal in partial implementation takes the same Oz LaTmura
-- addition (15%) as an existing one under (ו).
`a new principal of 52 in partial implementation` MEANS
    `upper-division employee` WITH
        `in the upper-division teaching-staff grade` IS TRUE
        `employed by an owner supervised by the Ministry` IS TRUE
        `implementation`                     IS `partial implementation`
        `role`                               IS `a principal`
        `appointed in 2012/13`               IS TRUE
        `age`                                IS 52
        `a mother`                           IS FALSE
        `a mother keeping the regular week`  IS FALSE
        `actual position`                    IS 1
        `position at all employers`          IS 1
        `matriculation preparation hours allotted` IS 0

`a new and an existing principal take the same addition` MEANS
    (`the new principal's additions` `a new principal of 52 in partial implementation`)'s `Oz LaTmura addition - principals`
    EQUALS `the Oz LaTmura addition rate` `a new principal of 52 in partial implementation`
#ASSERT `a new and an existing principal take the same addition`
#ASSERT `the principal's week in 2012/13` (`a new principal of 52 in partial implementation`'s `age`) EQUALS 37

`a partial-implementation mother of 56` MEANS
    `upper-division employee` WITH
        `in the upper-division teaching-staff grade` IS TRUE
        `employed by an owner supervised by the Ministry` IS TRUE
        `implementation`                     IS `partial implementation`
        `role`                               IS `a teacher`
        `appointed in 2012/13`               IS FALSE
        `age`                                IS 56
        `a mother`                           IS TRUE
        `a mother keeping the regular week`  IS TRUE
        `actual position`                    IS 0.8
        `position at all employers`          IS 1.35
        `matriculation preparation hours allotted` IS 1

#ASSERT `the position the salary is computed on` `a partial-implementation mother of 56` EQUALS 0.883
#ASSERT `within the position ceiling` `a partial-implementation mother of 56`
#ASSERT `the Oz LaTmura addition rate` `a partial-implementation mother of 56` EQUALS 21%
#ASSERT `the job base in 2012/13` `a teacher` 56 EQUALS 28
